Sval: open a window in the background, behind the window in front

Sval opens an agent's workspace window when a page in that workspace opens a
tab and no window shows the workspace, or when the agent acts and none is
open. That window must not take the keyboard from the user or cover the window
they are working in. Every platform's top-level Show activates and raises a
window whenever the app is in the foreground (nsCocoaWindow::Show's
makeKeyAndOrderFront, nsWindow::Show's SW_SHOWNORMAL under CanTakeFocus, GTK's
focus-on-map), and the only exceptions, alwaysontop and alert windows, float
above every other window, so no chrome API or window feature opens an ordinary
window behind. This adds a system-only "background" window feature,
CHROME_OPEN_IN_BACKGROUND, which the widget reads at its first show: macOS
orders the window below the app's key or main window, or behind every window,
without making it key; Windows shows it with SW_SHOWNOACTIVATE below the
foreground window; GTK asks the window manager not to focus it on map; the
headless widget does not activate it. BrowserWindowTracker files such a
window behind the window in front, so it is not taken for the user's top
window.

diff --git a/browser/modules/BrowserWindowTracker.sys.mjs b/browser/modules/BrowserWindowTracker.sys.mjs
index e1a8f6d8d2..3de804dc64 100644
--- a/browser/modules/BrowserWindowTracker.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/modules/BrowserWindowTracker.sys.mjs
@@ -147,7 +147,17 @@ var WindowHelper = {
       window.addEventListener(event, _handleEvent);
     });
 
-    _trackWindowOrder(window);
+    // Sval: a window opened in the background starts behind the one in front.
+    const background =
+      window.docShell.treeOwner
+        .QueryInterface(Ci.nsIInterfaceRequestor)
+        .getInterface(Ci.nsIAppWindow).chromeFlags &
+      Ci.nsIWebBrowserChrome.CHROME_OPEN_IN_BACKGROUND;
+    if (background && _trackedWindows.length) {
+      _trackedWindows.splice(1, 0, window);
+    } else {
+      _trackWindowOrder(window);
+    }
 
     // Update the selected tab's content outer window ID.
     _updateCurrentBrowserId(window.gBrowser.selectedBrowser);
